essbook><name>TAKAHASHI, MAMORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSURU, KAZUTAKA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUI, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJITA TERUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASAI TETSUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUKAWA NAOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO TETSUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITANI MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTSUZUKI SHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO JUNJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI MAMORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSURU KAZUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUI TOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJITA, TERUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASAI, TETSUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUKAWA, NAOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, TETSUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITANI, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSUZUKI, SHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, JUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, MAMORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSURU, KAZUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUI, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Ethylene (co)polymers excellent in moldability, mechanical characteristics and so on and suitable for various moldings, particularly pipes. For example, ethylene homopolymers or ethylene/C4-C20  alpha -olefin copolymers, wherein the number of methyl branches is less than 0.1 per 1000 carbon atoms as determined by &lt;13&gt;C-NMR and the Mw/Mn ratio is 1.8 or above but below 4.5 as determined by GPC; and ethylene homopolymers or ethylene/C3-C20  alpha -olefin copolymers, wherein the melt tension (MT) and the swelling ratio (SR) satisfy the relationship: log(MT) &gt; 12.9 - 7.15 x SR, and the intrinsic viscosity ([ eta ]) and the melt flow rate (MFR) satisfy the relationship: [ eta ] &gt; 1.85 x MFR&lt;-0.192&gt; in the case of MFR &lt; 1, or [ eta ] &gt; 1.85 x MFR&lt;-0.213&gt; in the case of MFR &gt;/= 1.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne des (co)polymères d'étylène se prêtant particulièrement bien au moulage, présentant d'excellentes caractéristiques notamment mécaniques et convenant particulièrement à la réalisation de moulages tels que les tuyaux. L'invention concerne essentiellement des homopolymères d'éthylène ou des copolymères d'éthylène ou d' alpha -oléfine en C4-C20. En l'occurrence, le nombre de branches méthyle est inférieur à 0,1 pour 1.000 atomes de carbone mesuré par RMN au &lt;13&gt;C, et le rapport Mw-Mn est d'au moins 1,8 tout en restant en dessous de 4,5 mesuré par chromatographie sur gel. L'invention concerne également des homopolymères d'éthylène ou des copolymères d'éthylène ou d' alpha -oléfine en C3-C20. En l'occurrence, la tension à l'état fondu (MT) et le coefficient de gonflement (SR) ont entre eux un rapport tel que log(MT) &gt; 12,9 7,15 x SR, la viscosité intrinsèque ([ eta ]) et l'indice de fluidité (MFR) ayant entre eux un rapport tel que [ eta ] &gt; 1,85 x MFR&lt;-0.192&gt; pour MFR &lt; 1, ou [ eta ] &gt; 1,85 x MFR&lt;-0.213&gt; pour MFR &gt;/= 1.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>